i'm excited to hear all the speakers and  learn about their perspective on the  topic that is dear to me i've been a  student of bioinformatics  all of my life so i'm excited that i'm  working with many of you here today on  making this discipline more accessible  it is also great to see as much as  broader rpc appreciation of data in the  life science domain as well as great  excitement about the potential impact of  bioinformatics on areas touching the  lives of everyone such as medicine  vaccine design genomic surveillance and  even space travel  so let me take this opportunity to  briefly introduce myself our team  since 20 2019 we have launched the omics  logic in india with initial  collaborations at several universities  where we piloted our training worked  with faculty to develop programs that  addresses the major gap in  bioinformatics education  so uh we saw that with the evident  evident of many uh breakthroughs in  molecular biology advances of  advancements in precision medicine uh  biotechnology and agriculture new  technologies were adopted in the  industry and research that  research that simplifies generation of  accurate and in-depth data  however a lack of analytical power  and a lack of analytic analytical power  and appropriate skills amongst  researchers and students  researchers and students created a huge  gap between data and information that is  needed in this field  so  the technical demand prevents that for  happening so uh  and that that limitation that limiting  ability to rely on techniques such as  rna sequencing genomic sequencing but  after working with many students at  universities in india we discovered even  more interesting insights that were  relevant today  so after many programs coordinating with  universities and thousands of students  across india we saw that there is a gap  in the skills that help students  effectively integrate  these studies into their research  projects thinking critically about data  and applying appropriate analysis  methods to the right data  so in most of these case studies in on  in most of these cases that meant  students were able uh were able to learn  develop independent research project in  a short period of time and get excited  about the opportunity and apply  bioinformatics in domains like oncology  neuroscience infectious diseases and  agriculture  so this overwhelming majority of  students were surveyed  pointed  to their interest to recommend such  trainings and integrate them into their  curriculum  and this is why i think all of this  makes sense and this is why we are here  today to discuss what can our education  system do about this gap how do schools  colleges and universities prepare  students for the future of biotechnology  life sciences in general where bio  biology is acquiring the characteristics  of data science so how we manage to do  this and how we are going to overcome  this is very important so this symposium  is extremely important for us and hope  you all are excited as we are to hear  about these challenges not from just us  from our team but from experts who have  spent their entire life struggling to  learn about these challenges and more  importantly come up with great solutions  so to tell you more about the symposium  so in the next two days we will hear  these speakers address these topics we  can all relate to so how to stand out  from a crowd when you apply for an  academic program or a career in  bioinformatics  what can universities  do to equip their students with relevant  skills and experiences  what is the future of this field where  will you find cutting-edge  challenges that you can contribute to  so we separated these topics into two  days uh the first day is about the  challenging role of bioinformatics in  research industry and education and the  second day is on how you can get  involved and make an impact  finally after the speakers present their  insights to us uh in the form of short  20 minute long presentations we will  have a chance to ask them about the  prospective on the future of  bioinformatics in india and if you have  any questions and i'm asking all of you  here  to ask your questions that you would  want to get answers  ahead of the  ahead and you can go ahead with the  symposium page and submit your questions  there as well as well as you can put  them in the chat i will ask our support  team to monitor our submissions and  prepare them for the panel discussion so  the panel discussion will start at 4 45  pm uh ist so that would be  almost 50 minutes from now after we have  the sessions uh from the mentors
 

